0..72 Comment "// A move hands a handle on whole and keeps its name: the one descriptor"
73..147 Comment "// leaves the mover\'s linear slot and enters the receiver\'s. No moved-from"
148..224 Comment "// object stays behind, as C++ leaves one \"in a valid but unspecified state\""
225..298 Comment "// for its destructor ([lib.types.movedfrom], ISO/IEC 14882:2020), and no"
299..374 Comment "// move constructor runs. Rust moves the same way, but a type\'s `Copy` impl"
375..449 Comment "// decides whether `let b = a;` moves or copies; here the handle is linear"
450..474 Comment "// wherever it is bound."
476..500 Comment "// The file\'s protocols."
